      YoMomma's Lister v1.3 written in 1996 AD by Black Widow/MiSERY

  -========================================================================-


 Introduction
--------------

   I first thought about writing this program simply because I couldn't find
any file listers at all for DayDream, and the users on my board were asking me
how to download the filelists, so I decided to write this.  From the kludge
it started out as, it's actually become quite a decent little program, so
I figured that at v1.3 it had enough features to be released to the public,
so here it is.


 FreeWare
----------

   This program is released as freeware for the whole DayDream SysOp
community.  Feel free to spread to as many places as you can.  The only thing
I ask is that if you use this door, please send me an E-Mail to the address
at the end of the doc.


 Disclaimer
------------

   Ok, this *shouldn't* fuck up, but if it does, I just want to say that I
take no responsability for anything this program might do.  Sorry, but if
shit happens it's your fault.  Use of this program implies the acceptance
of these terms.


 Features
----------

   This door basically allows users to download the filelists from file areas
on any BBS running DayDream.  It has several features, including:

      1 - Displays 'fileareas' file, either in conf/display/[mode] or 
          display/[mode] and adds on .GFX/.TXT as appropriate.

      2 - 4 available formats to download lists (LhA, LZX, ZIP, TXT),
          configurable by the user.

      3 - Allows to download a selected area, all areas or upload area.

      4 - Configurable temporary directory, for those short on memory.


   Not only that, but It's the only door I know of that does this, which is
a big plus. :)


 Installation
--------------

   Installation is quite simple.  If you've installed a door before, you
should have a vague idea.  If not, here goes:

  1 - Copy MSY-YML.EXE to doors:, MSY-YML.CFG to daydream:configs/ (or
      whereever your env:dreamutils points to).

  2 - Edit daydream.cfg (or your current config file) and include the
      following stub in the EXTERNALCOMMANDS.DAT (v1.20 and onwards):

		DOOR_COMMAND.. FLD
		DOOR_TYPE..... 1
		DOOR_SECURITY. 200
		DOOR_EXECUTE.. doors:MSY-YML.EXE %N
		DOOR_CONFS1... XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
		DOOR_CONFS2... XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

  3 - Compile the daydream.cfg using daydream/utils/dreamconfig.

  4 - Edit the config file to be to your taste.


 Usage
-------

   That's it from the SysOps point of view.  The user still has to configure
the program (which will be done the first time each user runs this program).
After this, the option 'Configure' is still available at the prompt.  Note
that you need enough memory available to run the archivers, or else the
door will freeze and a reset is necessary.


 Known Bugs
------------

   None so far, apart from the memory thing shown above, which isn't really
a bug.. :)


